# The seed corpus is generated, not source. `examples/gen_fuzz_corpus.rs` writes
# one named seed per case, and the `fuzz` lane runs it before it fuzzes, so the
# seeds cannot drift from the fixture builders that produce them — which is what
# happened while they were committed (A-SUPPORT-DECLARED). libFuzzer's own
# discoveries land here too, under their SHA-1, and are not seeds either: they
# are unbounded, hash-named and carry no intent.
corpus/
